            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0192" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">747.47H/12: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Australia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canberra</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-03T13:00:00+11:00">February 3, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 3—5:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. Reference Department’s 10, February 1, 6 p.m. I presented text of message to
                    Prime Minister Curtin at noon today. Apparently Minister External Affairs had
                    not informed Prime Minister of my conversation with him on January 21
                    communicating our ideas.</p>
                <p>Curtin authorized me to assure you that there is no immediacy involved in plan
                    for calling conference and stated that he would give me a considered reply
                    shortly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
